# VISUALRIF environment variables — names only, never commit values.
# Copy to .env.local for local development; set real values in Vercel project settings.
#
# Next.js foundation phase: no application environment variables are required.
# Vercel Web Analytics needs no keys (enabled in the Vercel dashboard).
#
# Vercel build setting (Vercel project env, not used by the app):
#   ENABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_COREPACK=1  — makes Vercel install with the pnpm version pinned in package.json "packageManager".
#
# Later phases will add variables here (Sanity, Attio, Resend, Turnstile, Redis, Sentry, search verification).
